# Autonomous Milestone Execution

## Post-0.1 (current default)

Do **not** autonomously start new feature phases. Follow
`.cursor/rules/post-0.1-development.mdc` / ADR-0020. Category 6 (new features)
needs a design/evidence report and explicit approval.

## Pre-0.1 charter track (legacy)

Only when actively executing an unfinished WEAVE.md milestone sequence:

### Continue automatically

When a charter milestone completes successfully, **immediately start the next
defined milestone**. Do not ask for permission to continue that charter.

### Decide locally for routine work

Make ordinary implementation choices without asking when they fit `WEAVE.md`
(structure, naming, tests, reversible details). Prefer the simplest sound option.

### Ask only when blocked

Ask only if a product/architectural choice is outside what `WEAVE.md` settles,
or progress needs credentials / irreversible external action.

## Override

Explicit user instructions always win over this rule. Post-0.1 development rule
wins over automatic next-phase continuation for feature work.
